# Keep the build context small and the image reproducible.
#
# node_modules matters most. The Dockerfile runs `npm ci` and THEN `COPY . .`;
# without this line, a developer machine with node_modules present would copy its
# own — built for that machine's platform — straight over the ones npm ci just
# installed for the image. The result builds on a laptop and fails in the image,
# or worse, works until a native module disagrees.
node_modules
dist

# Never let a local .env reach an image layer. Configuration is injected at run
# time by docker-compose; a copy baked into the image would be both stale and a
# secret sitting in a layer anyone who pulls the image can read.
.env
.env.*

coverage
*.log
.git
